 775			lem:ld-combining-exact-linearity, def:ld-combined-strategy}
 776		Let $\mathcal S$ be a projective strategy for the directly indexed game with
 777		parameters $\mathsf{ldparams}$, and let $G^{\mathrm A}$, $G^{\mathrm B}$ be
 778		measurements with outcomes in $\polyfunc{m+k}{q}{d}$ satisfying, for the
 779		combined strategy $\mathcal S^{\mathrm c}$ and with error $\delta$, the three
 780		conclusions of Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness} at parameters
 781		$\mathsf{ldparams}^{\mathrm c}$, using the relabeled point measurements of
 782		Definition~\ref{def:ld-combined-strategy}.  Let $H^w$ be $G^w$ post-processed by the
 783		map $\mathrm{split}$ of Lemma~\ref{lem:ld-combining-split}, so that
 784		$H^w \in \mathrm{PolyMeas}(m,q,d,k)$.  Then the three conclusions of
 785		Theorem~\ref{lem:ld-soundness} hold for $\mathcal S$ at parameters
 786		$\mathsf{ldparams}$, with the measurements $H^{\mathrm A}$, $H^{\mathrm B}$
 787		and with error $O(\delta + (m+k)d/q)$, where the point effects in the first
 788		two conclusions are $\widehat A^{\mathsf{Point},u}$ and
 789		$\widehat B^{\mathsf{Point},u}$, respectively.
